1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,982
Welcome to LUMI, The Dream Repair Atelier, built for haX.baby, Track 2: Your Own Baby.

2
00:00:06,982 --> 00:00:15,234
In this video we'll visit every page, from Home to the very last page, and try every feature along the way.

3
00:00:15,943 --> 00:00:17,532
This is the home page.

4
00:00:17,532 --> 00:00:25,187
Lumi is a tiny moon moth who mends broken dreams with moonlight thread and flies them home before sunrise.

5
00:00:25,187 --> 00:00:31,687
Watch her eyes: they follow your cursor wherever it goes. Click her, and her mood changes.

6
00:00:59,098 --> 00:01:06,075
Up in the header there's a mute switch. Sound always starts muted, and the site remembers your choice.

7
00:01:06,075 --> 00:01:12,847
Next to it, the Twilight and Midnight toggle changes the whole palette, and even Lumi's expression.

8
00:01:13,551 --> 00:01:18,101
Look closely at the moon. A hidden star is tucked into the sky.

9
00:01:18,101 --> 00:01:23,735
There are five of them across the site, and finding all five unlocks a secret.

10
00:01:24,436 --> 00:01:29,023
Scrolling down, the home page tells the whole story in one long page.

11
00:01:29,023 --> 00:01:33,743
Three quick answers explain what Lumi is, what she does, and her story.

12
00:01:33,743 --> 00:01:43,914
The Start Lumi's Journey checklist guides first-time visitors through the best two-minute path, and a little flying Lumi keeps you company as you scroll.

13
00:01:44,629 --> 00:01:48,900
The Meet Lumi page holds the five point character sheet:

14
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:57,213
her name, what she is, what she does, her story, and her tagline. Even the smallest light can rescue a dream.

15
00:01:57,917 --> 00:02:05,896
The mood switcher changes Lumi's face: happy, curious, focused, sleepy, and full of joy.

16
00:02:09,385 --> 00:02:18,722
Switch to 3D, and Lumi becomes a hand-built Three.js model. Drag to spin her around. Her lantern casts real light.

17
00:02:18,722 --> 00:02:21,589
And here is the second hidden star.

18
00:02:27,783 --> 00:02:33,005
The Story page tells Lumi's origin in four scroll-driven chapters.

19
00:02:33,005 --> 00:02:42,262
In chapter one, a fallen star has forgotten how to shine. Tap it, and Lumi's lantern wakes it up. Its name is Polara.

20
00:02:42,965 --> 00:02:47,989
In the next chapter, gather the scattered crystal shards into Lumi's satchel.

21
00:02:47,989 --> 00:02:53,013
The chapters carry on to the brass observatory where she builds her workshop.

22
00:02:53,013 --> 00:02:55,884
A third hidden star lives in this story too.

23
00:03:20,997 --> 00:03:27,071
At the end is Lumi and the Little Light, a bedtime storybook with 3D page turns.

24
00:03:27,071 --> 00:03:30,791
It works with buttons, swipes and the arrow keys.

25
00:03:31,494 --> 00:03:38,156
Now to Workshop No. 07, where you become Lumi's apprentice across three connected inventions:

26
00:03:38,156 --> 00:03:41,953
repair a dream, forge a lantern, and deliver it home.

27
00:03:42,663 --> 00:03:44,659
First, the Dream Repair Lab.

28
00:03:44,659 --> 00:03:53,287
Pick up each shard, Hope, Memory, Wonder and Courage, and place it in its matching slot to mend the broken dream crystal.

29
00:03:59,910 --> 00:04:02,497
Next, the Moonlight Lantern Studio.

30
00:04:02,497 --> 00:04:12,329
Name your dream, choose a vessel shape, a glass colour and a core symbol, turn up the glow, and pick a twilight or midnight backdrop.

31
00:04:12,329 --> 00:04:18,909
Then create a keepsake card you can download as an image. The fourth hidden star is here.

32
00:04:22,205 --> 00:04:24,633
Then the Dream Delivery Navigator.

33
00:04:24,633 --> 00:04:31,774
As you scroll, Lumi flies one continuous route across the map, lighting up each stop with its story.

34
00:04:33,993 --> 00:04:37,797
You can also choose a sleeper and send the dream yourself.

35
00:04:37,797 --> 00:04:44,029
Lumi flies the lantern home to the Cloud Garden, the Sleeping Lighthouse and Moonflower Valley.

36
00:04:44,029 --> 00:04:47,112
The fifth and final hidden star is on this map.

37
00:04:52,067 --> 00:04:57,101
The Night Playroom opens with the Lullaby Lab, a star-comb music box.

38
00:04:57,101 --> 00:05:03,302
Every tine plays a note made live with the Web Audio API, with no audio files at all.

39
00:05:03,302 --> 00:05:07,971
You can play Lumi's song, or record your own tune and replay it.

40
00:05:20,044 --> 00:05:26,034
Lantern Hide-and-Seek turns your cursor, your finger, or the arrow keys into Lumi's lantern.

41
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:31,243
Sweep the light across the dark dream layer to find four sleeping dream friends.

42
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:38,833
In Catch the Falling Dreams, steer Lumi to catch the dreams tumbling out of the sky.

43
00:05:38,833 --> 00:05:42,269
Every catch plays the next note of Lumi's lullaby.

44
00:05:51,193 --> 00:05:55,733
In the Dream Friend Maker, visitors sew their own companion:

45
00:05:55,733 --> 00:06:01,938
a ghost, a cloud, a robot, an alien, a monster, or a dreamy version of themselves.

46
00:06:01,938 --> 00:06:09,052
Choose a colour, a mood and an accessory, give it a name, and adopt it onto the nursery shelf.

47
00:06:14,450 --> 00:06:20,359
The Sleepers' Guestbook is a live, shared wish wall with a mechanical visitor odometer.

48
00:06:20,359 --> 00:06:23,347
Write a bedtime wish and pin it to the wall.

49
00:06:23,347 --> 00:06:29,664
Behind the scenes it is protected by rate limits, a honeypot for bots, and gentle moderation.

50
00:06:30,368 --> 00:06:32,949
From any page you can chat with Lumi.

51
00:06:32,949 --> 00:06:41,182
She answers in character, powered by Claude, and if the AI is ever unavailable she replies from her storybook instead.

52
00:06:42,906 --> 00:06:45,825
Click the lightning bolt for 90s Chaos Mode.

53
00:06:45,825 --> 00:06:55,245
The site becomes an early-web homepage with a scrolling marquee, classic badges and a webring, and it rearranges itself for every screen size.

54
00:07:00,122 --> 00:07:06,831
The last page is Goodnight, the ending of Lumi's story, where every mended dream is home and glowing.

55
00:07:07,714 --> 00:07:13,458
Because we found all five hidden stars, the secret constellation is complete.

56
00:07:13,458 --> 00:07:18,158
It unlocks a page from Lumi's secret diary, and a golden crown.

57
00:07:18,862 --> 00:07:23,981
Back on the home page, the journey checklist has noticed everything we did.

58
00:07:23,981 --> 00:07:28,691
And the footer credits every font, library and service the site uses.

59
00:07:29,394 --> 00:07:34,091
Finally, the Build Notes page explains how everything was made.

60
00:07:34,091 --> 00:07:44,007
LUMI works on phones, tablets and desktops, supports the keyboard throughout, and scores one hundred for accessibility on Lighthouse.

61
00:07:44,007 --> 00:07:48,032
Even the smallest light can rescue a dream. Goodnight!

62
00:07:50,254 --> 00:07:52,283
Thank you for watching.
